# A second REAL process on the same --out (the spec above uses a second `open()` of the same file in one process, which
# `flock` also treats as another owner). A holder process locks `--out/.mutate.lock` (`fcntl.flock(f, LOCK_EX)`, sleeps),
# then `scripts/gizmo-perf/mutate.py --phase prepare|time --out DIR` is started as a command, from the worktree
# (it never gets past the lock: no git, no rustc, no cargo, no measurement is asked for); then the holder is killed with SIGKILL.
